    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, it's probably just a pinhole leak. but man, it's just so frustrating because it's always in that same dark, narrow space underneath. i'll be staring at it with a flashlight and i swear i see something shift or a little shadow dart away into the corner of the base. \n\nit's making me wonder if there's something physically obstructing the sensor or the drain path that's just... lurking there. do you think it's possible for some kind of small, organic buildup or even a piece of something that looks almost like a little creature to get stuck in there and cause these weird 'mischievous' patterns?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
